# The BAKED half of ~/.ssh/config inside infra-dev. The entrypoint writes the real
# file as:
#
#     /run/infra-secrets/ssh_config.fleet    (zero, one, two — host-specific)
#     this file                              (github.com, then the wildcard)
#
# ORDERING RULE: ssh uses the FIRST value it obtains for each keyword, so specific
# blocks go at the top and the wildcard at the bottom. That is why the fleet blocks
# are prepended and not appended. (The opposite of sshd_config, where Match blocks
# must go last — easy to conflate.)
#
# WHY THE FLEET BLOCKS ARE NOT IN THIS FILE. They carry addresses, and this repo's
# own invariant is that host-specific values live in a gitignored file and never in
# tracked content. NOTHING WRITES THEM TODAY: fleet access is the deferred
# control-node question — docs/management-plane.md § "A control node inside the fleet" —
# so this file is, in practice, the whole of the container's ~/.ssh/config. The prepend
# is kept because it costs nothing and is the shape the answer would take.

# ── GitHub: none ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No github.com block since 2026-10-27: GitHub is reached over https with the hub's token
# for this repo alone (dev/README.md § "GitHub tokens, one repo each"), never over ssh.

# ── defaults — MUST stay last ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# IdentitiesOnly stops ssh offering every key it owns to every server it meets. The
# per-host IdentityFile lines above, and in the fleet blocks prepended before them,
# still win because they are obtained first.
Host *
  IdentitiesOnly yes
  ServerAliveInterval 30
  ServerAliveCountMax 3
